===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|lening}}, {{m|enm|leninge}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hlinung|t=leaning; resting; place of rest}}, equivalent to {{af|en|lean|-ing}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[tendency]] or [[propensity]].
#: ''a man of socialist '''leanings'''''

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|lenynge}}, {{m|enm|lenand}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*hliniende}} (suggested by {{cog|ang|hliniend|t=leaner, one who reclines}}), from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hlinjandz}}, present pariticple of {{der|en|gem-pro|*hlinjaną|t=to lean}}. Equivalent to {{af|en|lean|-ing}}.

